  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Periods of rain and breezy conditions from \nIsaias arrive tonight and continue through Sunday \n\nFair weather will be in play today with dry conditions and\nincreasing mid and high level clouds.Rain associated with \nIsaias is projected to reach the Laurel Highlands before \nmidnight tonight and gradually expand throughout central PA \ninto Sunday morning. Periods of rain continue Sunday afternoon \ninto Sunday night before tapering off by early Monday. Total \nrainfall amounts are still forecasted between 0.75 and 1.50 \ninches over a 24-36hr duration with a low risk of potential \nflooding impacts. \n\nAs post-tropical/TD Isaias tracks from the TN Valley into\nWV, gusty winds will overspread the Laurel Highlands with\nmaximum wind gusts of 35-45 mph west of the tallest ridges.\nElsewhere, gusts of 20 to 30 mph will be possible. Winds will \nincrease this evening, reaching gusts of up to 45 mph, before \ntapering off after 2 pm Sunday. A Wind Advisory has been issued \nfor Cambria and Somerset counties.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2: Trending warmer to start an unsettled week\n\nAfter the rain tracks off to the east, temperatures will begin\nto rise Monday. Clouds will begin to decrease later in the \nafternoon as air starts to trend drier. Tuesday a cold front\nwill drop south through the Commonwealth bringing a chance for\nshowers and an isolated thunderstorm or two. Wednesday will\nprovide brief reprieve before the next system moves over the\nstate Thursday as rainy weather settles in through the weekend.",
